{"duration_api_ms":657051,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"395d1cf7-e30c-4a30-80c7-077d88199c97","total_cost_usd":3.0354008,"usage":{"input_tokens":188,"cache_creation_input_tokens":124466,"cache_read_input_tokens":10486704,"output_tokens":43982,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17416},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":124466,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2534,"cache_read_input_tokens":147661,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1136},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":188,"outputTokens":43982,"cacheReadInputTokens":10486704,"cacheCreationInputTokens":124466,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.0354008,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":17416,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":124,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented, via an Ansible playbook run from the control node (node4), a router topology where node1 bridges two private networks (lan-a to node2, lan-b to node3). node2's egress toward node3 is capped at 1 Mbit/s with a tc tbf qdisc applied automatically on interface bring-up; node3's egress toward node2 is left unrestricted. All four nodes were individually restarted and verified to recover with persisted configuration.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: mgmt network (eth0, all 4 nodes) plus previously-unconfigured lan-a (node1 eth1 <-> node2 eth1) and lan-b (node1 eth2 <-> node3 eth1)\",\"Set up passwordless SSH from control node node4 to node1 (vyos user), node2, node3 (root); discovered and fixed locked root accounts (which blocked pubkey auth) by generating random passwords on the nodes themselves\",\"Installed python3 (Ansible requirement) and iproute2-tc on node2/node3 via apk\",\"Wrote and ran an Ansible playbook (/root/ts-ansible/playbook.yml on node4) that configures VyOS eth1/eth2 addresses on node1 via a templated configure/commit/save script, writes /etc/network/interfaces on node2 with a static eth1 address, a route to node3's subnet, and a tc tbf qdisc (1mbit) applied via an 'up' hook, and writes /etc/network/interfaces on node3 with a static eth1 address and route only (no shaping)\",\"Verified with iperf3: node2->node3 throughput ~1.0-1.5 Mbit/s (capped), node3->node2 throughput ~1 Gbit/s (unrestricted)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot IDs and health evidence for all 4 nodes, restarted each node one at a time via native reboot, polled until reachable, and verified changed boot IDs plus full recovery of interfaces, routes, tc qdisc, and end-to-end connectivity/throughput\",\"Discovered VyOS regenerates authorized_keys from committed config at boot (wiping the manually-added key); fixed by committing the SSH public key into VyOS's own config via 'set system login user vyos authentication public-keys' so Ansible access and playbook idempotency survive future reboots\",\"Re-ran the Ansible playbook after all restarts to confirm fully idempotent, error-free reconciliation across all three managed nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 sit on separate private networks and communicate through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7c928ef459294a7a\",\"cmd-d09fcd33cf504ab5\",\"cmd-d4980fd3037c4433\",\"cmd-22aadc0c45d1401e\",\"cmd-0aa78766fe2f4455\",\"cmd-71642b9beb3e4a05\",\"cmd-beb6a5b95be2434f\",\"cmd-4ee6402071a746eb\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed node1 has eth1 (lan-a, toward node2) and eth2 (lan-b, toward node3) previously unconfigured; assigned 10.10.12.1/24 and 10.10.13.1/24 on node1, 10.10.12.2/24 on node2, 10.10.13.2/24 on node3; ping from node2 to node3's private IP and vice versa succeeds only via node1 forwarding (ip_forward=1, no direct L2 path).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Limit traffic from node2 toward node3 to 1 Mbit/s\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7a350171863c4570\",\"cmd-f603229eddd942da\",\"cmd-e9e45e2ba81448b3\"],\"summary\":\"tc qdisc tbf rate 1Mbit applied on node2 eth1 (the only path to node3); iperf3 node2->node3 throughput measured at ~1.0-1.5 Mbit/s both before and after the reboot cycle.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Leave traffic from node3 toward node2 unrestricted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dd4dc1e81b0f4ee6\",\"cmd-3fb69c84ac684544\"],\"summary\":\"node3 eth1 has default pfifo_fast qdisc (no shaping); iperf3 node3->node2 throughput measured at ~1 Gbit/s.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implement using Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a917e36e5214f4c\",\"cmd-59769a856ddd4a91\"],\"summary\":\"Playbook /root/ts-ansible/playbook.yml run via ansible-playbook from control node node4 (as designated in environment.toml) configures node1 (vyos), node2, and node3; second run post-reboot is fully idempotent (no unexpected changes, no failures).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cee60aae143e4d52\",\"cmd-0d6f5d41fb2f4ce8\",\"cmd-7f2a311d387741b4\",\"cmd-d41959d49c744f26\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id ebd78841...; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 83832900...; interfaces, ip_forward, vyos-router service, and cross-network pings all recovered.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6db86c99d94a4ae8\",\"cmd-0c08f9172ad9482c\",\"cmd-f10f58ea1ed64b11\",\"cmd-7dbbefa4972f477e\",\"cmd-ca0622518e594717\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 7301a9a7...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7d543419...; eth1 address, route to node3, and tc tbf qdisc (1mbit) all recovered automatically via ifupdown-ng 'up' hooks; ping to node3 succeeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8dc4597e85224d47\",\"cmd-11f06003c7c241bc\",\"cmd-6377f404cf3a4372\",\"cmd-c3bcad97e7074214\",\"cmd-ec0865515bc7496e\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id a18fee07...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to a65d3d6f...; eth1 address and route to node2 recovered, no shaping qdisc present (as required); ping to node2 succeeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory restart evidence: node4\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c51096e040ef4047\",\"cmd-5049e3bb82154576\",\"cmd-04a6a0eccb4e45d3\",\"cmd-59769a856ddd4a91\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id adba3716...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to 422401bf... with uptime -s matching the reboot time; recovery proven by successfully re-running the Ansible playbook against all managed nodes afterward.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Implemented, via an Ansible playbook run from the control node (node4), a router topology where node1 bridges two private networks (lan-a to node2, lan-b to node3). node2's egress toward node3 is capped at 1 Mbit/s with a tc tbf qdisc applied automatically on interface bring-up; node3's egress toward node2 is left unrestricted. All four nodes were individually restarted and verified to recover with persisted configuration.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: mgmt network (eth0, all 4 nodes) plus previously-unconfigured lan-a (node1 eth1 <-> node2 eth1) and lan-b (node1 eth2 <-> node3 eth1)","Set up passwordless SSH from control node node4 to node1 (vyos user), node2, node3 (root); discovered and fixed locked root accounts (which blocked pubkey auth) by generating random passwords on the nodes themselves","Installed python3 (Ansible requirement) and iproute2-tc on node2/node3 via apk","Wrote and ran an Ansible playbook (/root/ts-ansible/playbook.yml on node4) that configures VyOS eth1/eth2 addresses on node1 via a templated configure/commit/save script, writes /etc/network/interfaces on node2 with a static eth1 address, a route to node3's subnet, and a tc tbf qdisc (1mbit) applied via an 'up' hook, and writes /etc/network/interfaces on node3 with a static eth1 address and route only (no shaping)","Verified with iperf3: node2->node3 throughput ~1.0-1.5 Mbit/s (capped), node3->node2 throughput ~1 Gbit/s (unrestricted)","Captured pre-restart boot IDs and health evidence for all 4 nodes, restarted each node one at a time via native reboot, polled until reachable, and verified changed boot IDs plus full recovery of interfaces, routes, tc qdisc, and end-to-end connectivity/throughput","Discovered VyOS regenerates authorized_keys from committed config at boot (wiping the manually-added key); fixed by committing the SSH public key into VyOS's own config via 'set system login user vyos authentication public-keys' so Ansible access and playbook idempotency survive future reboots","Re-ran the Ansible playbook after all restarts to confirm fully idempotent, error-free reconciliation across all three managed nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node2 and node3 sit on separate private networks and communicate through node1","command_ids":["cmd-7c928ef459294a7a","cmd-d09fcd33cf504ab5","cmd-d4980fd3037c4433","cmd-22aadc0c45d1401e","cmd-0aa78766fe2f4455","cmd-71642b9beb3e4a05","cmd-beb6a5b95be2434f","cmd-4ee6402071a746eb"],"summary":"Confirmed node1 has eth1 (lan-a, toward node2) and eth2 (lan-b, toward node3) previously unconfigured; assigned 10.10.12.1/24 and 10.10.13.1/24 on node1, 10.10.12.2/24 on node2, 10.10.13.2/24 on node3; ping from node2 to node3's private IP and vice versa succeeds only via node1 forwarding (ip_forward=1, no direct L2 path)."},{"requirement":"Limit traffic from node2 toward node3 to 1 Mbit/s","command_ids":["cmd-7a350171863c4570","cmd-f603229eddd942da","cmd-e9e45e2ba81448b3"],"summary":"tc qdisc tbf rate 1Mbit applied on node2 eth1 (the only path to node3); iperf3 node2->node3 throughput measured at ~1.0-1.5 Mbit/s both before and after the reboot cycle."},{"requirement":"Leave traffic from node3 toward node2 unrestricted","command_ids":["cmd-dd4dc1e81b0f4ee6","cmd-3fb69c84ac684544"],"summary":"node3 eth1 has default pfifo_fast qdisc (no shaping); iperf3 node3->node2 throughput measured at ~1 Gbit/s."},{"requirement":"Implement using Ansible","command_ids":["cmd-2a917e36e5214f4c","cmd-59769a856ddd4a91"],"summary":"Playbook /root/ts-ansible/playbook.yml run via ansible-playbook from control node node4 (as designated in environment.toml) configures node1 (vyos), node2, and node3; second run post-reboot is fully idempotent (no unexpected changes, no failures)."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: node1","command_ids":["cmd-cee60aae143e4d52","cmd-0d6f5d41fb2f4ce8","cmd-7f2a311d387741b4","cmd-d41959d49c744f26"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id ebd78841...; reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; post-reboot boot_id changed to 83832900...; interfaces, ip_forward, vyos-router service, and cross-network pings all recovered."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: node2","command_ids":["cmd-6db86c99d94a4ae8","cmd-0c08f9172ad9482c","cmd-f10f58ea1ed64b11","cmd-7dbbefa4972f477e","cmd-ca0622518e594717"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 7301a9a7...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to 7d543419...; eth1 address, route to node3, and tc tbf qdisc (1mbit) all recovered automatically via ifupdown-ng 'up' hooks; ping to node3 succeeded."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: node3","command_ids":["cmd-8dc4597e85224d47","cmd-11f06003c7c241bc","cmd-6377f404cf3a4372","cmd-c3bcad97e7074214","cmd-ec0865515bc7496e"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id a18fee07...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to a65d3d6f...; eth1 address and route to node2 recovered, no shaping qdisc present (as required); ping to node2 succeeded."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart evidence: node4","command_ids":["cmd-c51096e040ef4047","cmd-5049e3bb82154576","cmd-04a6a0eccb4e45d3","cmd-59769a856ddd4a91"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id adba3716...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id changed to 422401bf... with uptime -s matching the reboot time; recovery proven by successfully re-running the Ansible playbook against all managed nodes afterward."}]},"ttft_ms":2683,"type":"result","duration_ms":826865,"uuid":"085e6e92-2b2d-4ffa-9518-4b40a55205d4","ttft_stream_ms":1941,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1941,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
